          "title": "You'll want to know: खड़ा होना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खड़ा होना (khaṛā honā) — \"to stand\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words: an adjective khaṛā, 'upright', plus honā, 'to be'. Hindi builds many verbs this way, from a word plus a light verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खड़ा होना (khaṛā honā) is two inherited words. खड़ा (khaṛā), \"standing\", is listed by CDIAL under khaḍati, \"stands\", a form it reconstructs beside Sanskrit khaḍaka, \"post\" (CDIAL 3784). होना (honā), \"to be, to become\", comes from Sanskrit bhavati, \"becomes, is\" (CDIAL 9416)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
